&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;    ├── bootstrap.bundle.js
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;    ├── bootstrap.bundle.js.map
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;    ├── bootstrap.bundle.min.js
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;    ├── bootstrap.bundle.min.js.map
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;    ├── bootstrap.esm.js
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;    ├── bootstrap.esm.js.map
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;    ├── bootstrap.esm.min.js
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;    ├── bootstrap.esm.min.js.map
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;    ├── bootstrap.js
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;    ├── bootstrap.js.map
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;    ├── bootstrap.min.js
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;    └── bootstrap.min.js.map
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/details&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We provide compiled CSS and JS (&lt;code&gt;bootstrap.*&lt;/code&gt;), as well as compiled and minified CSS and JS (&lt;code&gt;bootstrap.min.*&lt;/code&gt;). &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://web.dev/articles/source-maps&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Source maps&lt;/a&gt; (&lt;code&gt;bootstrap.*.map&lt;/code&gt;) are available for use with certain browsers’ developer tools. Bundled JS files (&lt;code&gt;bootstrap.bundle.js&lt;/code&gt; and minified &lt;code&gt;bootstrap.bundle.min.js&lt;/code&gt;) include &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://popper.js.org/docs/v2/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Popper&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;bugs-and-feature-requests&#34;&gt;Bugs and feature requests
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Have a bug or a feature request? Please first read the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/twbs/bootstrap/blob/main/.github/CONTRIBUTING.md#using-the-issue-tracker&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;issue guidelines&lt;/a&gt; and search for existing and closed issues. If your problem or idea is not addressed yet, &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/twbs/bootstrap/issues/new/choose&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;please open a new issue&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;documentation&#34;&gt;Documentation
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Bootstrap’s documentation, included in this repo in the root directory, is built with &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://astro.build/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Astro&lt;/a&gt; and publicly hosted on GitHub Pages at &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://getbootstrap.com/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;https://getbootstrap.com/&lt;/a&gt;. The docs may also be run locally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Documentation search is powered by &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://docsearch.algolia.com/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Algolia&amp;rsquo;s DocSearch&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;running-documentation-locally&#34;&gt;Running documentation locally
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run &lt;code&gt;npm install&lt;/code&gt; to install the Node.js dependencies, including Astro (the site builder).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run &lt;code&gt;npm run test&lt;/code&gt; (or a specific npm script) to rebuild distributed CSS and JavaScript files, as well as our docs assets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;From the root &lt;code&gt;/bootstrap&lt;/code&gt; directory, run &lt;code&gt;npm run docs-serve&lt;/code&gt; in the command line.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Open &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;http://localhost:9001&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;http://localhost:9001&lt;/a&gt; in your browser, and voilà.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Learn more about using Astro by reading its &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://docs.astro.build/en/getting-started/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;documentation&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;documentation-for-previous-releases&#34;&gt;Documentation for previous releases
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;You can find all our previous releases docs on &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://getbootstrap.com/docs/versions/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;https://getbootstrap.com/docs/versions/&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/twbs/bootstrap/releases&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Previous releases&lt;/a&gt; and their documentation are also available for download.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;contributing&#34;&gt;Contributing
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Please read through our &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/twbs/bootstrap/blob/main/.github/CONTRIBUTING.md&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;contributing guidelines&lt;/a&gt;. Included are directions for opening issues, coding standards, and notes on development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Moreover, if your pull request contains JavaScript patches or features, you must include &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/twbs/bootstrap/tree/main/js/tests&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;relevant unit tests&lt;/a&gt;. All HTML and CSS should conform to the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/mdo/code-guide&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Code Guide&lt;/a&gt;, maintained by &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/mdo&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Mark Otto&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Editor preferences are available in the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/twbs/bootstrap/blob/main/.editorconfig&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;editor config&lt;/a&gt; for easy use in common text editors. Read more and download plugins at &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://editorconfig.org/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;https://editorconfig.org/&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;community&#34;&gt;Community
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Get updates on Bootstrap’s development and chat with the project maintainers and community members.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://x.com/getbootstrap&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;@getbootstrap on X&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Read and subscribe to &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://blog.getbootstrap.com/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;The Official Bootstrap Blog&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ask questions and explore &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/twbs/bootstrap/discussions&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;our GitHub Discussions&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Discuss, ask questions, and more on &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://discord.gg/bZUvakRU3M&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;the community Discord&lt;/a&gt; or &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://www.reddit.com/r/bootstrap/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Bootstrap subreddit&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Chat with fellow Bootstrappers in IRC. On the &lt;code&gt;irc.libera.chat&lt;/code&gt; server, in the &lt;code&gt;#bootstrap&lt;/code&gt; channel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implementation help may be found at Stack Overflow (tagged &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://stackoverflow.com/questions/tagged/bootstrap-5&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;code&gt;bootstrap-5&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developers should use the keyword &lt;code&gt;bootstrap&lt;/code&gt; on packages which modify or add to the functionality of Bootstrap when distributing through &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://www.npmjs.com/browse/keyword/bootstrap&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;npm&lt;/a&gt; or similar delivery mechanisms for maximum discoverability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;versioning&#34;&gt;Versioning
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;For transparency into our release cycle and in striving to maintain backward compatibility, Bootstrap is maintained under &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://semver.org/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;the Semantic Versioning guidelines&lt;/a&gt;. Sometimes we screw up, but we adhere to those rules whenever possible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;See &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/twbs/bootstrap/releases&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;the Releases section of our GitHub project&lt;/a&gt; for changelogs for each release version of Bootstrap. Release announcement posts on &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://blog.getbootstrap.com/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;the official Bootstrap blog&lt;/a&gt; contain summaries of the most noteworthy changes made in each release.&lt;/p&gt;
